id: pm-beads-y6cp
title: Explain invalid Beads dependencies with bounded row repair packets
description: "Overlap checked against beads validate, core relationship analytics, pm-graph analytics, and pm-csv provenance. This adds Beads JSONL row addresses and exact external identities plus revalidated edge-removal proposals. It does not replace core topology or CSV cell provenance."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-beads#188"
created_at: "2026-10-28T19:31:55.419Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T21:47:52.333Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A cycle involving three of 10000 rows returns those rows and edges within declared input, work and output budgets; every emitted candidate revalidates; malformed and unresolved references remain explicit gaps; no title-based identity inference."
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T19:32:23.416Z",codex-agent,"Overlap: beads validate already reports invalid JSON, dangling blockers and cycle messages; pm-graph owns workspace analytics; pm-csv owns table provenance. Use core RelationshipGraph and analyzeRelationshipExecution over opaque row tokens to preserve case-sensitive external identities. Add a read-only repair packet, bounded candidate edge removals, explicit gaps and source-byte revision guards. No tracker writes, journals or role-based lifecycle decisions are added."
  "2026-10-28T19:47:49.245Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: typed read-only packet and preview APIs, canonical CLI plus alias, lazy public graph SDK loading, exact UTF-8 source revision guard, isolated row gaps, integer work/input/output ceilings, and bounded fully revalidated edge-removal candidates. Targeted numeric/alias/extreme-value corpora and 512 seeded graph operation sequences compare an independent transitive-closure model, preserve every untouched native field, replay older inputs and verify native state read back through the real SDK. Existing import/export/transfer/reconciliation/outgoing model suites remain in the unchanged CI full gate. Behavioral revert in a disposable non-git copy suppressed only the new cycle witness; the 10000-row regression failed (expected one cycle, got zero). New module measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Follow-up required for previously ignored blocks-only provider rows; repair keeps them explicit gaps."
  "2026-10-28T19:49:13.653Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: public unbraind/pm-beads main a5946b1dc8ab1f2d33b0c84c81e5eb34be3073b2, tracker tree c0e59199996b59f0f10cbbf51ac8758a9fb5589a. Frozen non-git public copy: 109 rows, 69941 UTF-8 JSONL bytes, 0 native blocker edges/cycles/gaps. Baseline including lazy SDK startup: 670.67 ms. Synthetic in-memory cycle only: 3 row witnesses, 3 cycle edges, 1 revalidated corrective edit, 2 core analyses, 1132 compact JSON bytes, 41.88 ms. No git executable; tracker byte fingerprint and SDK-read state unchanged. Reproduce with node test/public-repair-validation.ts. Related follow-up pm-beads-np1y tracks blocks-only representation semantics."
  "2026-10-28T19:57:05.870Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary review added a shared producer/consumer schema for saved candidates: exact keys, dense bounded edit arrays, finite safe integer coordinates, exact string identities, no accessor or serialization-hook authority, and canonical field ordering. UTF-8 decoding preserves BOM bytes for SDK/CLI revision agreement. Final focused command: npm run build && npm run build:test && npm run docstring && node --test --test-concurrency=2 --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=repair.ts test/repair.test.ts. Result: 9 passed, zero skipped; repair.ts measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Additional metadata/docstring/flag tests: 13 passed. Linked pm test runs use pm-context none with workspace-context snapshot; source workspace plus none is correctly refused by the host. Native health passes with no extensions; extension-enabled local health has pre-existing pm-github host-version skew (pinned 2026.10.24 versus global extension 2026.10.28). No dependency pins or existing history were changed."
  "2026-10-28T20:04:21.968Z",codex-agent,"Final malformed-row corpus also covers unsafe title/name values before invoking the existing validator. An object-valued title with a non-callable toString is retained as an isolated invalid_record gap alongside usable cycle witnesses. Existing validate/import coercion is tracked separately by pm-beads-4kw8; blocks-only semantics remain pm-beads-np1y. Final focused suite: 9 passed, zero skipped, 100% lines/branches/functions; the 10000-row cycle case completed in 2551.76 ms including preview. Final public-copy replay preserved the same 109 rows and 69941 bytes: baseline 865.49 ms, synthetic cycle 77.45 ms, 1132 compact packet bytes, one validated edit, unchanged frozen tracker and SDK-read state."
  "2026-10-28T20:07:12.490Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passed on all 5 paths (npm global, Bun global, project-local, npx, bunx), host 2026.10.28, same 55-file artifact, SHA-256 d1d327cf5b5a17c3ea3dc402358fcbe7f47b0e8a8ed26886ecd594f2deb15190; artifact bytes unchanged after all invocations. Reproduce with node test/packed-repair-acceptance.ts. Final public-copy measurement after all boundary changes: 109 rows, 69941 JSONL bytes, baseline 311.44 ms, synthetic three-row cycle 28.69 ms, 1132 compact packet bytes, three edges and one revalidated edit; tracker fingerprint and SDK-read state unchanged. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix; exact-head run URLs and counts will be included in the PR before handoff. Claim released for orchestrator review; items intentionally remain open."
  "2026-10-28T20:12:30.838Z",codex-agent,"Post-push bounded-work review: initial structural checks now reuse the producer beadTitle normalizer directly rather than invoking the full legacy validator over an invalid graph. This removes an unbudgeted second cycle enumeration; all topology is owned by bounded core analyses. The full existing validator remains mandatory on the corrected acyclic candidate. Rerunning focused coverage, exact packed acceptance and public-copy validation; final CI must use the new head."
  "2026-10-28T20:20:18.803Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 40760622195 at 2ed0e24: all 537 tests passed in the Node 26 Bun gate, but its aggregate coverage was 99.96% because an existing index.ts silent-child-stderr fallback branch was not exercised. Added a deterministic typed-error check using the existing CLI spawn seam; no SDK mocks and no lowered threshold. New repair module was 100% in that gate. Final head will rerun both npm and Bun gates after the bounded-analysis adjustment."
  "2026-10-28T20:25:08.216Z",codex-agent,"Final follow-up validation: bounded repair analysis still passes all 9 focused tests with 100% lines/branches/functions. Deterministic list/refusal suite passes 59 tests. Updated public read-only copy: 109 rows, 69941 JSONL bytes, baseline 334.96 ms, synthetic 3-row/3-edge cycle 32.87 ms, one revalidated edit and 1132 compact JSON bytes; native SDK state and tracker fingerprint unchanged. Packed retry now shares an isolated npm cache across global/local/npx installs and allows 240 seconds for launcher setup after a cold npx preparation timeout; current receipt will be published in the PR before handoff. Source implementation is complete; final exact-head npm/Bun gates remain required. GitHub REST is temporarily rate-limited, so status/PR evidence will use available read and GraphQL surfaces. Claim released for orchestrator review; no item closed."
  "2026-10-28T20:39:40.884Z",codex-agent,"CI wait cutoff reached: source head 70cd5d87251d1971d8cbd8bbd01872bdb6b8a28d, run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40763604922 still has test (22) and test (26) queued, so 0 of 4 final npm/Bun gates completed and final full-suite counts are unavailable. Stop waiting under the 30-minute queue rule; keep PR 188 ready for orchestrator verification. Current code has passing npm-global, Bun-global and project-local packed cases; focused npx and bunx also passed using the verified cached CLI 2026.10.28 after cold-cache setup failures. Focused current artifact: 55 files, SHA-256 2e8f29dc397ac95eb2ce6388a6582aefe5974b1c7b51900658cba53e067f6bea, 3 witness rows, 3 edges and 1 candidate through both launchers in non-git trackers. No native state changed. Local targeted totals: 9 repair tests, 59 workspace-refusal tests and 13 metadata/flag/docstring tests passed; repair.ts 100% lines/branches/functions. Feature claim is released; pm-beads-np1y and pm-beads-4kw8 remain open follow-ups. This final receipt commit changes tracker evidence only; its fresh CI status must remain pending until verified."
  "2026-10-28T20:56:39.284Z",codex-agent,"Continuation of PR 188 after reading its body and existing evidence. Merged origin/main first. General rule: never serialize an untrusted JSON row through JavaScript numbers; edits preserve unchanged source bytes, including duplicate keys and numeric lexemes. Audit every JSON parser/serializer in repair, sidecar, reconcile, transfer, outgoing and native import/export; exercise SDK, JSON/TOON CLI, packed npm/Bun launchers and non-git trackers. One blocking finding supplied; GitHub reviews contain no additional actionable non-blocking findings. Existing item stays open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-28T21:02:57.709Z",codex-agent,"Package-wide precision audit: repair editedText was the direct whole-row round trip; sidecar restore was a second row reserializer, and sidecar parse/capture could silently round long decimal literals. Shared syntax-validated JSON source spans now retain untouched row bytes and surviving dependency object tokens, including foreign overflowing exponents. Sidecar restore retains existing field text; its version 1 numeric envelope refuses nonrepresentable new literals before output, while accepting equivalent decimal spellings and previously emitted canonical envelopes. Reconcile, transfer and outgoing reserialize documented schema projections of native fields, strings, revisions and integer counts rather than preserved opaque source rows; native export serializes SDK-owned mapped rows. JSON and TOON repair receipts contain only bounded witness coordinates and exact string identities. New 512-sequence source-byte oracle passed, including beyond-2^53 integers, negative zero, overflowing/underflowing exponents, long decimals, duplicate foreign and dependency keys, CRLF, escapes and surviving edge metadata. Added the two-worker ceiling to the coverage runner without changing thresholds."
  "2026-10-28T21:05:14.271Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable non-git source copies: fixed 512-sequence byte property passed; restoring only the old repair removeEdge/editedText serializer failed at sequence 0 on foreign_revision 9007199254740993; fixed restore passed again. Restoring only the old sidecar restore function failed the literal native-priority spelling/whitespace assertion. Restoring only the old sidecar parseJson function failed the required long-decimal precision refusal. Restored fixed sidecar passed. No existing tests or thresholds weakened. Existing focused repair/sidecar suites: 45 passed, 0 skipped. Compiled CLI byte previews passed both JSON and TOON extreme-value cases; corrected the new test baseline to read state through SDK get, because SDK create omits get-only collection-count fields."
  "2026-10-28T21:09:23.560Z",codex-agent,"Linked-test execution note: the inherited test provenance points to the PR branch, while the required new worktree uses a distinct local continuation ref because that branch is already checked out. The host correctly refused that inherited linked command as foreign_source_ref. The continuation-added test command has this worktree provenance and is running with pm-context none and workspace-context snapshot; no testing policy or historical provenance was rewritten. Native strict health with extensions disabled passes. New shared JSON source module independently measured 100% lines, branches and functions."
  "2026-10-28T21:11:30.056Z",codex-agent,"Current public read-only validation after merging main: public source e27eec6178aa89a13165104304254e7e6c3c8938, tracker tree 16c0a347b8927bfb2b54c891d36206a554ae8626, 110 rows, 70404 JSONL bytes, zero native blocker edges/cycles/gaps. Baseline including lazy SDK load: 409.87 ms; synthetic in-memory 3-row cycle: 3 witnesses, 3 edges, 1 revalidated edit, 2 core analyses, 1132 compact JSON bytes in 149.64 ms. Tracker byte fingerprint and complete SDK-read state unchanged with read-only files, no git executable and a non-git tracker. Direct new precision suites passed all 6 tests with no skips; the separate existing repair/sidecar suites passed 45. Combined all numeric extremes into each CLI fixture so both output formats cover every lexeme in one invocation per format; separate 512-sequence SDK tests still exercise each value independently."
  "2026-10-28T21:45:02.978Z",codex-agent,"Final source-boundary follow-up preserves all separator whitespace when deleting scalar aliases: only property tokens and required commas are removed. Literal tests cover first/middle/last/adjacent/all duplicate keys plus untouched scalar/array aliases. Final shared module: 100% lines, branches and functions. Repeated disposable behavioral reverts on final source: fixed repair precision plus whitespace tests 2/2 passed; old repair serializer 0/2 passed; restored 2/2. Old sidecar restore failed literal preservation; old parseJson failed precision refusal; fixed restored sidecar passed. Local full npm release check used two workers and hit the existing 900-second coverage bound with ETIMEDOUT; no full-suite result is claimed. Per the original host-resource instruction, full npm/Bun evidence will come from fresh CI, with the same two-worker runner. Existing strict native health passes with extensions disabled; extension-enabled local health retains the previously documented pm-github/host 2026.10.28/2026.10.24 skew. Production audit found zero vulnerabilities; release workflow, docstrings, pack dry-run, publish-attestation, release-date and changelog checks pass. No SDK pins, coverage thresholds, existing test assertions or history records were weakened or rewritten."
  "2026-10-28T21:47:45.842Z",codex-agent,"Final artifact receipt: 59 shipped files, SHA-256 fb2ada2ffe24edd54f6962ae6edb3609f05bfa21d17896ad433d164d807f75b4; exact artifact bytes unchanged across npm-global, Bun-global, project-local, npx and bunx. All five real launchers passed both JSON and TOON receipts and consumed them through the packed SDK preview, preserving beyond-2^53 integers, negative zero, overflowing exponents, long decimals, duplicate keys and CRLF; native SDK-read tracker state and source files stayed unchanged. Final continuation-owned linked test ran through pinned pm with snapshot workspace and no PM context: 6 passed, zero skipped, including all 512 literal-byte properties and the final whitespace/alias cases. Existing focused repair/sidecar corpus: 45 passed. Three independent final behavioral revert proofs are recorded above. Package and native checks are complete; exact-head full npm/Bun CI under Node 22 and 26 remains required because the loaded-host full npm run reached ETIMEDOUT at its existing 900-second bound. Final CI run URL and full counts will be reported in PR 188 and the handoff. Claim released after these receipts; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification, with no merge or release."
